  "item3_root_cause": "Relay B (Substation B L1-21) is fed from CT 52-L1 core 1 landed on the full winding X1-X5 = 2000:5 (ratio 400; commissioning record Sub B 2023-04-14, DWG B-E-2214), while the relay is set CTR = 240 (1200:5, tap X2-X4) as the settings calculation requires. Relay B measures 240/400 = 0.60 of the true current, so every apparent impedance is 1.667x too large and the reverse zone Z3R (1.74 ohm sec) did not reach the reverse BC fault on L2. With no Z1, Z2 or Z3R and RX from relay A (Z2 keying for the L2 fault in its overreach), the echo AND held for EDPU = 32 samples and relay B echoed the permissive back; relay A then tripped by POTT (Z2 AND RX). The tap error became exposed when ECHO was enabled at B in settings revision R5 (2026-05-26).",
